  "body": "The lanes view drew a stripe as one rect per logged day, each inset a pixel top and bottom with rounded corners, so every day boundary opened a ~2px window onto the page background. Spawn connectors draw *behind* the stripes, so a connector crossing a lane showed through those windows — a crossing read as if it terminated in the stripe instead of passing under it.\n\nA stripe is now one shape per unbroken run of days. Boundaries are drawn on top of the fill as an opaque seam in a darker cast of the day's own colour, with a matching outline around the run. Days still read as cells in a bar — that segmentation is what makes the length countable — but the separation is paint rather than a hole, so nothing can pass through it.\n\n- Per-day rects survive as invisible hit targets over the fill, so a click still opens exactly one date's entry and a hover still names one day.\n- Bridged (unlogged) days merge into a single thin bar, for the same reason: a run of them used to draw as a row of ticks when the narrowing is meant to read as one constriction.\n- Connectors now land on the middle of their first day instead of its top edge. That edge is exactly where a boundary seam sits, so a workout spawning mid-run and a day boundary were drawing the same mark at the same height.\n\nVerified by rendering the running app headless at 1280x1000 and reading the PNG: the 2-day pink stripe reads as one segmented bar, and the teal connector stops at its left edge and re-emerges on the right.",
  "changed_files": 1,
